From: Cubie A7S robot project
Subject: [PATCH] a733: throttle at 90C, gpu as a cooling device

The board dts sets the cpu zones' throttling target to 60C, the same as its
fan trips. Without a fan the cpus then sat at 416MHz whenever the die was
over 60C, idle included. Throttle at the soc's own 90C and leave the fan
trips alone, so a fan starts at 60C and the clocks only drop when the fan
isn't enough, or isn't there.

The img gpu driver only registered a devfreq cooling device when the platform
gave it power ops, which sunxi doesn't, so the dt's gpu trips had nothing to
throttle. Register it without a power model.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board/vendor tuning]
---
diff -ru a/device-a733/configs/cubie_a7s/linux-6.6/board.dts b/device-a733/configs/cubie_a7s/linux-6.6/board.dts
--- a/device-a733/configs/cubie_a7s/linux-6.6/board.dts	2026-11-11 20:43:24.151458344 +0100
+++ b/device-a733/configs/cubie_a7s/linux-6.6/board.dts	2026-11-11 20:46:03.565630215 +0100
@@ -842,8 +842,9 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/* fan trips stay at 60C, throttling waits for the soc default 90C so fanless boards keep their clocks */
 &cpul_target {
-	temperature = <60000>;
+	temperature = <90000>;
 	hysteresis = <2000>;
 };
 
@@ -865,7 +866,7 @@
 };
 
 &cpub_target {
-	temperature = <60000>;
+	temperature = <90000>;
 	hysteresis = <2000>;
 };
 
diff -ru a/bsp/modules/gpu/img-bxm/linux/rogue_km/services/server/env/linux/pvr_dvfs_device.c b/bsp/modules/gpu/img-bxm/linux/rogue_km/services/server/env/linux/pvr_dvfs_device.c
--- a/bsp/modules/gpu/img-bxm/linux/rogue_km/services/server/env/linux/pvr_dvfs_device.c	2026-11-11 20:43:24.156479186 +0100
+++ b/bsp/modules/gpu/img-bxm/linux/rogue_km/services/server/env/linux/pvr_dvfs_device.c	2026-11-11 20:46:11.764508129 +0100
@@ -965,11 +965,9 @@
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
+	/* no power ops: a plain state cooling device, step_wise still throttles it */
 	if (!powerOps)
-	{
-		dev_info(dev, "Cooling: power ops not registered, not enabling cooling");
-		return 0;
-	}
+		dev_info(dev, "Cooling: no power ops, registering without a power model");
 
 	of_node = of_node_get(dev->of_node);
 
